Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat: restore community/rubric/grading redesign, perf
 fixes and toolbar labels
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rebuilt the working tree after the temporary checkout was cleared by a
reboot; the two earlier commits had not been pushed.

Content restored from the previous rounds:
- community list redesign (tabs, status chips, sort, right rail)
- simplified rubric workbench and grouped rubric viewer
- dimension-level grading panel with collapsed fine-tuning
- inline/block math, figure annotations, outline numbering
- HTTP compression, immutable caching for hashed assets, N+1 query fixes
- copy trimming across dashboard, evidence, progress and review pages

New in this commit:
- jumpToFeedback now expands the collapsed panel and any enclosing
  <details> before scrolling, so clicking an annotation always lands on
  the right card
- editor toolbar shows text labels (加粗 … 代码) and gains a code-block
  button; undo/redo/export/help are labelled too
- editor heading left block flexes to fill its row instead of collapsing
  to a narrow strip with a large empty gap
